# HSM collector conformance v1 — sampled bar partial-post contract (#1428). Wall-clock fixture.
# Format: case|action|arg1|arg2|...
# Actions introduced here:
# create_sampled_double_bar_sensor|path|bar_period_ms|bar_tick_ms|post_period_ms|precision
#   A DoubleBar whose samples come from a driver-owned source (the n-th sample is n), taken every
#   bar_tick_ms into a bar of bar_period_ms, with a partial of the in-progress bar posted every
#   post_period_ms. This is the machinery behind the metric-driven default bars (Total CPU, Free RAM,
#   Process CPU/memory/threads — managed BarMonitoringSensorBase via CollectableBarMonitoringSensorBase;
#   native metric-source binding) with fixture-sized periods; the catalog runs 5 min / 5 s / 15 s.
# expect_bar_open_times_nondecreasing
# expect_partial_bars_accumulate
#   Payloads sharing an OpenTime are snapshots of one bar: same CloseTime and First, Count never
#   shrinking in delivery order.
# expect_bar_posts_sharing_open_time_at_least|min
# expect_distinct_bar_open_times_at_least|min
# Contract notes:
# - Partial posts keep the bar's OpenTime until the window closes; the server overwrites same-OpenTime
#   partials and persists one bar per bar period (not one per post).
# - The window is aligned to multiples of the bar period; a new OpenTime appears after the boundary.
# - Stop flushes the in-progress partial bar.
# - Periods divide the 0001->1970 epoch offset (README "Determinism"), and every assertion is a
#   timing-immune invariant: the exact number of samples per post depends on scheduler jitter.

# 4.6 s over 2 s windows with 0.5 s posts: at least one window is covered end to end, so at least
# three posts (at +0.5 s, +1 s, +1.5 s) share its OpenTime, and at least two windows appear.
sampled_bar_partial_posts_share_open_time|create_collector
sampled_bar_partial_posts_share_open_time|create_sampled_double_bar_sensor|contract/sampled/partial|2000|100|500|2
sampled_bar_partial_posts_share_open_time|start
sampled_bar_partial_posts_share_open_time|sleep_ms|4600
sampled_bar_partial_posts_share_open_time|stop
sampled_bar_partial_posts_share_open_time|expect_all_bars_aligned|2000
sampled_bar_partial_posts_share_open_time|expect_bar_open_times_nondecreasing
sampled_bar_partial_posts_share_open_time|expect_partial_bars_accumulate
sampled_bar_partial_posts_share_open_time|expect_bar_posts_sharing_open_time_at_least|3
sampled_bar_partial_posts_share_open_time|expect_distinct_bar_open_times_at_least|2

# With the post period and the window both an hour away, the only payload is the Stop flush of the
# partial bar, holding the source's first sample.
sampled_bar_stop_flushes_partial|create_collector
sampled_bar_stop_flushes_partial|create_sampled_double_bar_sensor|contract/sampled/flush|3600000|100|3600000|2
sampled_bar_stop_flushes_partial|start
sampled_bar_stop_flushes_partial|sleep_ms|400
sampled_bar_stop_flushes_partial|stop
sampled_bar_stop_flushes_partial|expect_sent_count|1
sampled_bar_stop_flushes_partial|expect_bar_field|0|type|5
sampled_bar_stop_flushes_partial|expect_bar_field|0|first|1
sampled_bar_stop_flushes_partial|expect_bar_field|0|min|1
sampled_bar_stop_flushes_partial|expect_bar_open_close_aligned|0|3600000
